# Server charge of a domain retry top-up

The server the top-up counts is the customer's active server with auto-renew on when its next auto-renew attempt falls before the retry; a server has no retry days, so its single attempt day is the server charter's renewal day before its term end. Because every auto-renew charge in any category tries credit first, the top-up covers this charge in full when its next auto-renew attempt falls from today up to the day before the retry, which credit would otherwise pay first. Where the product's account discount applies, its charge is reduced by the account tier's server discount, the discount being the charge less the reduced charge rounded half up to the cent. The server charge of the top-up follows its billing term:

- 24-month term: the product's 24-month price per month times 24;
- 12-month term: the product's 12-month price per month times 12;
- 1-month term: the product's 1-month price per month;
- otherwise: no server charge is counted.

The charge so found enters the credit the retry needs.

*Hypothetical:* a 12-month server at $14.20 per month: $170.40; with a 7 percent server discount, $158.47.

*Applies to: Harborline Customer Accounts, for the customer's server on VPS and Dedicated Servers*
